  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The baseline TiVNbTa alloy is a single-phase BCC dendritic material.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline TiVNbTa has a room-temperature yield strength of approximately 800 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, baseline TiVNbTa has approximately 330 MPa yield strength, 423 MPa compressive strength, and about 30% strain.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 0.5–1 at.% carbon during TiVNbTa processing is the proposed intervention.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A 0.5–1 at.% carbon addition will enable controlled in situ carbide precipitation in TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled-atmosphere arc melting or powder metallurgy will ensure homogeneous carbon distribution.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A subsequent heat treatment can be selected to nucleate nanoscale carbide precipitates.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting structural mediator will be uniformly dispersed, fine, coherent carbide nanoparticles, such as TiC, in a BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7",
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon will react with Ti or other reactive elements during solidification or heat treatment to form stable nanoscale carbides.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbide precipitates will impede dislocation motion and produce precipitation hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7",
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Precipitation hardening will increase the high-temperature yield and compressive strengths of TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7",
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coherency between the carbides and matrix will limit the loss of ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coherent carbide precipitates will preserve the thermal conductivity needed for heat transfer between W and CuCrZr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-modified TiVNbTa will exhibit approximately 20–30% higher yield and compressive strengths at 1273 K than baseline TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::rubric_card::000::c40db9eaa7",
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-modified TiVNbTa will retain more than 30% strain at 1273 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon addition will not significantly reduce thermal conductivity.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed material is intended to operate under tensile and compressive loading at temperatures up to approximately 1273 K.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
